0..79 Comment "//! A flow between types written as the relation `A ⇝ B`, also `A ~~> B`: the"
80..164 Comment "//! type-level spelling of `Flow[.A = Type](A, B)`, introduced by `Flow.into` over a"
165..241 Comment "//! translator. Under directed univalence a flow between types is a function"
242..313 Comment "//! [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory],"
314..393 Comment "//! Definition 1.2, so `⇝` abbreviates the flow itself and no record of round"
394..421 Comment "//! trips stands beside it."
